virglrenderer: shader constants through uniform buffers, one upload per submit

What: CONST[0] (a guest shader's plain uniforms, sent with SET_CONSTANT_BUFFER) becomes
the uniform block <prefix>constblk { uvec4 <prefix>const0[n]; } instead of the uniform
array <prefix>const0[n]. Before a submit is decoded, the payloads of its
SET_CONSTANT_BUFFER commands are copied into one staging block (vrend_const_prescan,
vrend_decode.c calls it); the first of them that runs uploads the block with one
glBufferData into the next of four buffers of the sub context. A vertex shader reads
its constants through a window: its block holds GL_MAX_UNIFORM_BLOCK_SIZE bytes, its
references become <prefix>const0[virgl_cbase + i], and virgl_cbase is an int vertex
attribute at the last location (glBindAttribLocation, never an array), so a draw sets
one attribute value (glVertexAttribI1i) and binds the window only when its constants
lie outside the bound one. Other stages, and vertex shaders that use every attribute
location, bind their range per draw with glBindBufferRange (as vrend already does for
the VirglBlock). Constants that did not come through the upload (another sub context in
the same submit, a ring buffer that took a later submit, fewer constants than the shader
reads) go into the stage's own buffer, zero-padded, on the draw that needs them. Only
where the block fits: desktop GL with uniform buffers, not compute, at most
GL_MAX_UNIFORM_BLOCK_SIZE, and room for this block and the VirglBlock in the stage's
uniform block limit; other shaders keep the uniform array.
OMACVM_VIRGL_CONST_UBO=0 keeps every shader on uniforms (the code path from before),
=1 binds a range per draw in vertex shaders too; qemu.log says which at start.
OMACVM_VIRGL_CACHE_STATS=1 logs uploads, binds, index draws and window binds.
Why: Apple's GL redoes much of its draw setup after any glUniform call, whatever its
size (~0.53 us per draw on an M4 Max), and WebGL pages change uniforms before nearly
every draw (Aquarium 30k: ~31,000 SET_CONSTANT_BUFFER + draws a frame, QEMU's render
thread at 98 %). In the host-only measurement (bench/aquarium-fusion/drawcost-const.c)
a range bound per draw cost 0.19 us less per draw, a window plus an index attribute
0.35 us less.
Upstream: not sent (depends on OmacVM's uniform block checks).
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-const-ubo.c (soft GL + gl-oracle; per-draw constants in each
stage, stale ring buffers, short constants, an index in the shader, program and sub
context switches, a guest uniform buffer in the same shader, a cut-off command, a window
that moves, a vertex shader without a free location; run in all three modes),
Tests/virgl/index-range-writes.py (the new buffer writes are vrend's own).

